Package: crake
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: dorhawk.software <ondrej@dorhawk.software>
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://dorhawk.software
Depends: @SHLIBS@, nftables, iproute2, systemd-resolved | systemd (<< 252), polkitd | policykit-1, dbus, openconnect | openvpn | openvpn3
Recommends: openvpn, gnome-shell-extension-appindicator, gnome-keyring
Suggests: openvpn3
Description: VPN client that routes only what needs the tunnel
 Crake connects to AnyConnect-compatible gateways (and the other protocols
 openconnect speaks) and to OpenVPN profiles, routes nothing by default,
 and learns per host what needs a tunnel: a host that doesn't answer
 directly but answers through a tunnel is sent through just that tunnel.
 Several tunnels can be up side by side. Everything it decides happens on
 this computer; nothing is sent anywhere.
